Package: NaileR
Title: Evidence-First Interpretation of Statistical Profiles with AI
Version: 2.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nel", "Hervé", role = "aut"),
    person("Sébastien", "Lê", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sebastien.le@institut-agro.fr",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8814-6714"))
    )
Description: Combines statistical evidence produced by 'FactoMineR' and
    'SensoMineR' with large language models to support interpretation of
    continuous variables, categorical groups, contingency-table profiles,
    sensory product profiles, and grouped open-ended text. Rebuilt analyses
    retain canonical evidence artifacts separately from model prompts and
    responses, allowing statistical evidence, generated prompts, and raw model
    responses to be inspected through a common user-facing interface. Local
    'Ollama' models and Google 'Gemini' are supported.
